WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:15.154
Zann didn't have to think very hard about his decision.

2
00:00:15.174 --> 00:00:17.356
"Sorry," he told Venna.

3
00:00:17.756 --> 00:00:19.097
"I have to help my friend."

4
00:00:19.898 --> 00:00:20.358
"Let's go."

5
00:00:20.758 --> 00:00:21.879
Teplo sounded pleased.

6
00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:23.381
"I have a plan in mind."

7
00:00:24.121 --> 00:00:26.823
"You're making a mistake, Zann," Venna warned.

8
00:00:27.284 --> 00:00:28.445
"Magica needs you."

9
00:00:29.145 --> 00:00:30.366
"Gliss needs me too."

10
00:00:30.887 --> 00:00:32.088
Zann walked toward the door.

11
00:00:32.884 --> 00:00:34.285
Venna glanced at her assistants.

12
00:00:35.026 --> 00:00:36.006
Zann held his breath.

13
00:00:36.366 --> 00:00:37.507
Would she try to stop him?

14
00:00:38.668 --> 00:00:39.068
She didn't.

15
00:00:40.049 --> 00:00:44.572
Soon Zann, Perda, Darb, Zing, Teplo, and Fala were outside.

16
00:00:44.592 --> 00:00:46.353
"What's your plan?"

17
00:00:46.653 --> 00:00:47.754
Perda asked Teplo.

18
00:00:48.415 --> 00:00:52.157
The old man pulled a hat out of his cloak, jamming it over his red hair.

19
00:00:52.938 --> 00:00:54.439
He tossed another hat to Zann.

20
00:00:55.219 --> 00:00:56.840
"I'll tell you on the way to the zoo."

21
00:00:56.860 --> 00:01:02.404
"Your plan sounds crazy," Perda told Teplo.

22
00:01:03.052 --> 00:01:04.213
"Can it really work?"

23
00:01:04.633 --> 00:01:06.154
They had been walking for twenty minutes.

24
00:01:06.174 --> 00:01:07.475
"Of course."

25
00:01:07.856 --> 00:01:09.056
Teplo sounded confident.

26
00:01:09.837 --> 00:01:12.899
"I've known much crazier plans to work perfectly."

27
00:01:13.660 --> 00:01:14.660
Fala looked dubious.

28
00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:19.484
"That's an awful lot of magic for one person—even a Magic Master.

29
00:01:20.204 --> 00:01:21.705
Do you think you can handle it?"

30
00:01:22.826 --> 00:01:25.808
"I haven't used any magic in days," Teplo said.

31
00:01:25.828 --> 00:01:27.690
"I'm rested and ready."

32
00:01:27.710 --> 00:01:29.691
"Hush!" Darb whispered.

33
00:01:29.711 --> 00:01:30.712
"More trolls."

34
00:01:31.584 --> 00:01:34.285
They ducked into a doorway and waited for the trolls to pass.

35
00:01:35.306 --> 00:01:37.587
Every second felt like an hour to Zann.

36
00:01:37.607 --> 00:01:39.728
"Are we almost there?"

37
00:01:40.108 --> 00:01:40.568
he whispered.

38
00:01:41.268 --> 00:01:41.929
Fala nodded.

39
00:01:41.949 --> 00:01:42.769
"Follow me.

40
00:01:43.209 --> 00:01:44.350
I know a secret way in."

41
00:01:45.570 --> 00:01:47.711
Soon they were pushing through a thick hedge.

42
00:01:48.392 --> 00:01:51.533
They peered out at the zoo, which was swarming with trolls.

43
00:01:51.553 --> 00:01:54.755
"The dragon pen is over there," Fala whispered.

44
00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:57.396
Zann had been to the zoo as a little kid.

45
00:01:58.028 --> 00:02:02.331
He remembered staring at the menacing wild dragons inside their iron-barred cage.

46
00:02:03.112 --> 00:02:06.574
Even knowing that the pen was a vacuum hadn't made the dragons less scary.

47
00:02:07.735 --> 00:02:09.136
Now the cage looked the same.

48
00:02:09.816 --> 00:02:12.358
But it was crammed full of people instead of dragons.

49
00:02:12.378 --> 00:02:13.979
"There's Gliss!"

50
00:02:14.379 --> 00:02:15.060
Darb whispered.

51
00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:18.022
Zann spotted their friend among the other prisoners.

52
00:02:18.742 --> 00:02:20.824
She was sitting on a rock, looking nervous.

53
00:02:20.844 --> 00:02:25.607
"It looks as if the trolls have captured every Red in First City!"

54
00:02:25.927 --> 00:02:26.548
Perda whispered.

55
00:02:27.552 --> 00:02:28.193
"Not quite."

56
00:02:28.533 --> 00:02:30.154
Teplo stared past the pen.

57
00:02:30.174 --> 00:02:31.935
"Here comes one more."

58
00:02:32.976 --> 00:02:36.338
A troll carrying an elderly woman stomped toward the cage.

59
00:02:37.079 --> 00:02:38.360
Darb glanced at Fala.

60
00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:41.041
"You said they needed only one more prisoner."

61
00:02:41.061 --> 00:02:43.843
"There's no time to waste," Zann said.

62
00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:46.105
"Teplo's plan might not be perfect.

63
00:02:46.785 --> 00:02:49.567
But even a crazy plan is better than none, right?"

64
00:02:50.308 --> 00:02:51.028
Teplo grinned.

65
00:02:51.048 --> 00:02:52.509
"That's the spirit, my boy!

66
00:02:53.210 --> 00:02:55.932
Let's see if we can get closer while they're distracted."

67
00:02:56.956 --> 00:03:00.740
Most of the other trolls were watching the one troll try to wrestle the new Red into the

68
00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:04.543
pen. Teplo dashed across the open area beside the pen.

69
00:03:05.204 --> 00:03:06.445
Zann and the others followed.

70
00:03:07.066 --> 00:03:11.269
When they reached the shelter of some shrubs, Teplo started fishing around inside his cloak.

71
00:03:11.289 --> 00:03:15.233
"Are you sure you can manage all that magic at once?"

72
00:03:15.653 --> 00:03:16.334
Fala asked him.

73
00:03:16.354 --> 00:03:19.657
"It'll require a tremendous amount of energy."

74
00:03:19.677 --> 00:03:22.480
"I could help," Zann offered.

75
00:03:23.104 --> 00:03:28.606
"Combine my energy with yours, take some of the smaller spells "Thank you, Zann.

76
00:03:28.707 --> 00:03:30.127
But no," Teplo said.

77
00:03:30.147 --> 00:03:32.728
"You don't have the experience for this type of magic.

78
00:03:33.529 --> 00:03:34.849
Besides, it's far too risky."

79
00:03:35.529 --> 00:03:39.611
Teplo pulled a large, lumpy turnip out of his cloak and tossed it into the grass.

80
00:03:40.312 --> 00:03:43.273
By the time it settled near the dragon pen, he'd pulled out more.

81
00:03:44.293 --> 00:03:46.634
Soon dozens of turnips dotted the ground.

82
00:03:47.815 --> 00:03:50.396
The trolls had finished locking away the new prisoner by now.

83
00:03:51.132 --> 00:03:55.616
Most of them wandered away, grunting loudly at one another as if discussing what to do next.

84
00:03:56.417 --> 00:03:59.840
The only troll that noticed the turnips was the one left guarding the prisoners.

85
00:04:00.661 --> 00:04:04.224
It stared at the vegetables with a look of dull confusion on its face.

86
00:04:05.004 --> 00:04:07.466
Teplo rubbed his hands together until sparks flew.

87
00:04:07.487 --> 00:04:10.129
"Animate," he murmured.

88
00:04:11.190 --> 00:04:13.992
The turnips started growing larger and larger.

89
00:04:14.713 --> 00:04:18.036
Then they changed shape, taking on human form.

90
00:04:18.764 --> 00:04:22.266
Within seconds they looked just like the Reds inside the pen!

91
00:04:22.967 --> 00:04:25.569
There was even one that looked exactly like Gliss.

92
00:04:25.589 --> 00:04:28.170
"Hurry," Fala hissed.

93
00:04:28.190 --> 00:04:33.274
"You have to hide the real prisoners, or they'll figure it out—even trolls aren't that dumb!"

94
00:04:34.054 --> 00:04:34.775
Teplo nodded.

95
00:04:34.795 --> 00:04:36.836
Beads of sweat dotted his face.

96
00:04:37.777 --> 00:04:40.899
But he rubbed his hands even harder and pointed at the pen.

97
00:04:40.919 --> 00:04:42.820
"Cloak," he muttered.

98
00:04:43.821 --> 00:04:47.944
Suddenly it was as if a sheer curtain had been dropped over the entire pen.

99
00:04:48.684 --> 00:04:52.247
The Cloaking spell dimmed the view of the prisoners but didn't hide them completely.

100
00:04:52.267 --> 00:04:54.669
"More!" Fala urged.

101
00:04:54.689 --> 00:04:55.710
"Let me help you!"

102
00:04:55.730 --> 00:04:57.611
"No—let me."

103
00:04:58.132 --> 00:04:59.213
Zann pushed past her.

104
00:04:59.853 --> 00:05:04.117
Grabbing Teplo's hands, he rubbed his own against them, joining their friction together.

105
00:05:04.137 --> 00:05:06.919
"Not safe!"

106
00:05:07.759 --> 00:05:10.201
Teplo gasped, his face drenched in sweat.

107
00:05:10.842 --> 00:05:13.224
But he didn't pull away as Zann focused his energy.

108
00:05:13.884 --> 00:05:19.052
Zann was good at Cloaking spells; he used them frequently to play tricks on Zing.

109
00:05:19.072 --> 00:05:20.053
"Hide," he muttered.

110
00:05:20.073 --> 00:05:22.175
"It's working!"

111
00:05:22.515 --> 00:05:23.135
Perda whispered.

112
00:05:23.996 --> 00:05:25.457
Zann pulled his hands away.

113
00:05:26.498 --> 00:05:28.119
The Cloaking spell was complete.

114
00:05:28.939 --> 00:05:31.541
The pen appeared to be completely empty!

115
00:05:32.402 --> 00:05:35.404
At the same time, Teplo's turnip army started to move.

116
00:05:36.545 --> 00:05:39.467
The old man was still creating friction as fast as he could.

117
00:05:40.228 --> 00:05:42.769
As he did, the fake Reds started running around.

118
00:05:43.490 --> 00:05:46.072
The guard troll was still staring in amazement.

119
00:05:46.812 --> 00:05:48.493
"Isn't it going to warn the others?"

120
00:05:48.893 --> 00:05:49.513
Perda wondered.

121
00:05:49.533 --> 00:05:55.115
"Maybe in about an hour,” Zann said, “when its brain catches up to its eyes."

122
00:05:55.135 --> 00:05:57.456
"We can't wait that long."

123
00:05:57.857 --> 00:05:59.737
Fala glanced anxiously at Teplo.

124
00:06:00.438 --> 00:06:02.178
He was groaning and sweating with effort.

125
00:06:02.198 --> 00:06:03.659
"You'd better do something."

126
00:06:04.419 --> 00:06:05.600
Teplo glanced at Zann.

127
00:06:05.620 --> 00:06:08.521
"Can you do a Sound-Shifting spell?"

128
00:06:08.841 --> 00:06:09.281
he asked.

129
00:06:10.101 --> 00:06:10.742
Zann gulped.

130
00:06:11.102 --> 00:06:13.343
He remembered studying that type of spell in school.

131
00:06:14.023 --> 00:06:16.104
But he hadn't been paying much attention that day.

132
00:06:17.105 --> 00:06:20.414
"Yes." Perda spoke up, holding out her hands to Zann.

133
00:06:20.434 --> 00:06:21.698
"He can.

134
00:06:22.159 --> 00:06:22.621
I'll help."
